  "evidence": [
    "Complete genuine Strings pointer-interface closure, with disjoint worker edit scopes and centrally coordinated shared headers. Combine every core/caller draft before a compiling checkpoint; intermediate raw workers are not accepted recovery.",
    "Pinned Strings::get6169A0 unsigned address-range validation: argument<=base returns base; base<argument<=target32 wrapped(base+size) returns argument; above end returns null. Endpoint inclusive. Stripped catalogue int spellings are not original type proof. Strings::put/text_item_string and rule fields produce LPSTR.",
    "Core API is Strings::get(LPSTR), parse_say second argument LPSTR with int return unchanged, and Label::strings_ptr LPSTR*. labels_init allocates count*4 and stores text_string pointers. Migrate pointer producers, local carriers and all raw byte-offset slot loads to typed index offset/4. No int overload, compatibility wrapper or cast-only workaround; genuine label_get indices remain integers.",
    "Preserve original call/read ordering, unsigned wrap, guards, null/low fallback, above-range null, all unsafe/error behavior and shared storage/lifetimes. No deliberate bug fixes. Evidence-backed ABI address-comparison casts and original all-bits-one pointer sentinel are permitted, not arbitrary numeric pointer fallbacks.",
    "Preserve all original identities/spans/claims/roles and useful historical LEVER/TRIED/binding findings. No hand markers, symbol guesses or BYTE_EXACT tokens. Worker ordinary C++/tests only, no Git/native/Wine/delegation/outside-scope edits. Coordinator uses native writers after fresh emitted symbol evidence; matching regressions retain restoration obligations.",
    "Manual integration needs independent actual-source/pinned-flow review, complete application build/link, relevant behavioral/mutation controls, scoped native comparisons, source/history continuity and references. This is not automatic/full-game acceptance. Nonlocal discoveries require central scope expansion, never silent omission.",
    "Probe source get62/getchoice/getF9 are translation errors: pinned5A08ED..0904 readsLabels+1010 (index404) before popupID62;5A0986..0998 reads Facility[choice].name via stride48;5A09EA..09FE readsLabels+3E4 (indexF9). Use correct label/member pointers and keep popup item IDs. NetDaemon project_name_id/related_name_id are Facility.name pointer carriers. Correct helper locals/Label indices throughout this group, preserving dialog/protocol behavior. Actual-source controls distinguish pointer operands from old numeric inputs."
  ],
